export anchor ObservatoryStyle:
    number: 320
    screen: OpsMonitor
    name: Observatory
    idea: A night observatory console where the last 24 hours are a round sky chart with traffic as a glowing contour and events as numbered marks on the rim, beside monospaced telescope readouts for each service.
    base: dark
    palette:
        nightSky: #04060d, the page with a sparse field of tiny stars
        console: #0a0f1e, panels and the style sheet
        consoleRaised: #111833, list rows
        ink: #e7ecff, text
        muted: #9ea9c9, labels, axis and times
        graticule: #26304d, borders, dashed rings and rules
        instrumentCyan: #7fd4ff, the traffic contour, object names, deploy stars, p50, the current app, buttons and panel corner ticks
        starGold: #ffd27a, the peak star, the incident ID, p95, Degraded and Investigating
        nightRed: #ff8b8b, the error line, firing and spike marks, Firing words and focus
        healthy: #8be0b0, Healthy and Resolved with circle and square
        recovered: #a8ccff, Recovered with a diamond
    type:
        Body in ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas at 14px and 1.55.
        Titles in Futura, Century Gothic, Trebuchet MS at 600 in caps,
        panel titles 13px tracked 0.22em, the sheet title 22px tracked
        0.16em. The incident ID is 24px mono in gold, readings 22px mono,
        axis and dial labels 10 to 11px mono.
    layout:
        A header with a thin telescope mark, BRIGHTWORK OPS in tracked
        geometric caps over a mono line production window 24 h, and the
        suite apps in a bordered segmented strip with Ops filled cyan. A
        two column grid follows. Left is the 24 hour sky panel, a round
        polar chart where time runs clockwise from 10 yesterday at the top,
        dashed rings mark 2.5k to 10k requests per minute, and the traffic
        contour is a translucent cyan shape widest at the afternoon peak
        with a gold peak star. Numbered marks sit on two rims, deploy stars
        inside and alert shapes outside, and a key plus a numbered Rim
        events list explain them. Right is a Service readouts table with
        Object, Status, Uptime and Reading columns in mono, then Incident
        under watch as a definition list with INC-0427 in gold and two
        buttons. A full width row of three strips holds Error rate, Latency
        and an Observation log of alerts and deploys. Panels are near opaque
        with cyan corner ticks at top left and bottom right. Below 1000px the
        columns stack, below 760px the strips stack and the readout table
        scrolls inside its panel.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px gutter and gaps, 18 by 20px panel padding, 10px table cell padding.
    density: Medium dense. A large dial, a five row readout table and three strips.
    corners: 2px panels and controls. The dial and swatches are round.
    borders: 1px graticule borders with cyan corner ticks, dashed rules between rows.
    shadows: None. Panels sit nearly opaque over the star field.
    icons:
        A thin telescope mark. On the dial, four point stars for deploys,
        squares for resolved, an octagon for firing and a triangle for the
        error spike, each numbered. In text, filled circle, triangle,
        diamond, octagon and square, and a magnifier, with the word.
    focus: A 2px night red outline offset 3px with a faint red halo.
    tone: Instrument log terms such as 24 hour sky, Service readouts, Object, Reading and Incident under watch.
